course: dictionary
lesson: 13213
title: Furrowed: fields and frowns
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Furrowed has two meanings, and the words around it show you which one to use. A furrowed field has long, narrow trenches cut into it by a plough. «The farmer's plough furrowed the wet field in straight lines.» The field is not sad or cross; it has been dug into neat lines ready for seeds.
explain: A furrowed brow means a forehead with deep lines in it. People get these lines when they worry, feel cross or think very hard. «Badger sat by the fire with a furrowed brow, trying to solve the puzzle.» The clue is the puzzle: he is thinking hard, not feeling happy.
explain: Ask yourself: is this thing a field or a face? Then swap in a simple word. A furrowed field is a ploughed field. A furrowed brow is a wrinkled brow. If your meaning fits the sentence, you have found the right one.
fact: A furrow is a long, narrow trench cut into soil by a plough.
fact: «Furrowed» can describe a field with trenches cut into it, or a brow wrinkled with deep lines.
fact: «He furrowed his brow» means he made lines across his forehead by frowning or thinking hard.
fact: Furrow can be a noun (a furrow in the field) or a verb (to furrow the soil, or to furrow your brow).
fact: Context helps: look for words like plough, seeds, worry or puzzle to show which meaning is right.
exercise: «The plough furrowed the field in long, straight lines, ready for seeds.» What does furrowed mean here? | Was painted bright green | *Had long, narrow trenches cut into it | Was made smooth and flat | Was covered in deep snow
exercise: «Mum's furrowed brow told me she was worried about the bills.» What does a furrowed brow show? | Joy at a party | Sleepiness after lunch | *Worry
exercise: «He furrowed his brow over the hard maths question.» What is he doing? | Dancing around the room | Sleeping in his chair | *Thinking very hard | Eating his lunch
test: «The furrows in the ploughed field were ready for the seeds.» What are furrows? | Small ponds full of rain | Piles of hay in the barn | Tall grass growing by the road | *Long, narrow trenches cut in the soil
test: «Badger sat with a furrowed brow, puzzling over the map.» What does the furrowed brow show? | Hunger before dinner | Being very cold | *Careful, hard thinking | Great happiness
exam: Which sentence uses furrowed to mean a wrinkled forehead? | *«She furrowed her brow at the sad news.» | «The tractor furrowed the soil.» | «The garden was full of bright flowers.» | «The fields were furrowed in spring.»
